WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.758 --> 00:00:12.979
Once upon a time, there lived an old fisherman and his wife.

2
00:00:13.719 --> 00:00:16.640
They lived in a modest hut on a small island.

3
00:00:19.501 --> 00:00:22.622
Every day the fisherman went fishing with his net.

4
00:00:24.702 --> 00:00:29.804
Usually he did not catch many fish, but one day his luck changed.

5
00:00:31.428 --> 00:00:32.188
"Oh my!"

6
00:00:32.588 --> 00:00:36.210
the fisherman exclaimed as he started to haul in his heavy net.

7
00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:39.450
"I must have caught an enormous fish!"

8
00:00:41.471 --> 00:00:44.832
But when the fisherman looked in the net, he was stunned.

9
00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:51.514
The heavy net was empty, except for one tiny golden fish.

10
00:00:53.295 --> 00:00:55.855
The fisherman peered more closely at the fish.

11
00:00:57.336 --> 00:01:01.086
Suddenly the creature opened its mouth, startling the man.

12
00:01:01.106 --> 00:01:03.227
"Please do not kill me!"

13
00:01:03.727 --> 00:01:05.068
the golden fish pleaded.

14
00:01:05.088 --> 00:01:09.871
"Return me to the sea and I will do whatever you wish."

15
00:01:09.891 --> 00:01:13.353
"This is no ordinary fish!"

16
00:01:13.753 --> 00:01:15.114
the old man realized.

17
00:01:15.935 --> 00:01:17.856
He took pity on the small creature.

18
00:01:17.876 --> 00:01:20.578
"I am content," he said.

19
00:01:20.598 --> 00:01:22.879
"I do not need anything from you.

20
00:01:23.279 --> 00:01:24.360
Go back to the sea."

21
00:01:26.468 --> 00:01:31.691
At home the fisherman's wife asked, as she always did, "Did you catch anything today?"

22
00:01:32.872 --> 00:01:33.992
The fisherman shrugged.

23
00:01:34.012 --> 00:01:36.694
"Nothing but a small golden fish."

24
00:01:37.774 --> 00:01:42.577
Then the fisherman told his wife about the extraordinary golden fish in his net.

25
00:01:43.177 --> 00:01:49.541
When the man relayed that he had let the golden fish go, his wife's face darkened with fury.

26
00:01:49.561 --> 00:01:51.122
"You fool!"

27
00:01:51.582 --> 00:01:52.342
she bellowed.

28
00:01:52.362 --> 00:01:55.084
"That was a magic fish!

29
00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:56.681
Why did you let it go?

30
00:01:57.241 --> 00:02:00.724
Why did you not wish for something—like bread for us to eat?"

31
00:02:02.025 --> 00:02:05.267
The wife reprimanded her husband all night long.

32
00:02:06.708 --> 00:02:10.791
Finally the fisherman couldn't stand his wife's complaints anymore.

33
00:02:11.651 --> 00:02:14.573
He returned to the sea to look for the magic fish.

34
00:02:14.593 --> 00:02:19.157
"Little fish, little fish," the man called out.

35
00:02:21.158 --> 00:02:23.660
Soon the golden fish swam to the shore.

36
00:02:24.992 --> 00:02:26.713
"What do you want, old man?"

37
00:02:26.733 --> 00:02:31.316
"My wife is very angry," the fisherman said.

38
00:02:31.336 --> 00:02:34.058
"She wants me to ask you for something."

39
00:02:35.039 --> 00:02:35.999
"What does she want?"

40
00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:37.280
asked the fish.

41
00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:41.263
"She wants bread," replied the man.

42
00:02:41.283 --> 00:02:44.945
"You gave me my life," answered the fish.

43
00:02:44.965 --> 00:02:49.388
"Go home and you will find what your wife wished for."

44
00:02:49.829 --> 00:02:51.189
Then it swam away.

45
00:02:52.991 --> 00:02:57.430
When the man returned to his hut, he asked, "Do we have bread now?"

46
00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:02.193
"We have plenty of bread now," his wife informed him.

47
00:03:02.213 --> 00:03:07.597
"But our hut is in disrepair and about to collapse!

48
00:03:08.578 --> 00:03:12.020
Return to the golden fish and demand a fine new cottage!"

49
00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:18.384
"Little fish, little fish," the man called out.

50
00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:23.008
Soon the golden fish swam to the shore.

51
00:03:23.884 --> 00:03:25.445
"What do you want, old man?"

52
00:03:25.465 --> 00:03:28.547
"My wife is discontent.

53
00:03:29.087 --> 00:03:32.809
Now she wants a fine new cottage," the man answered.

54
00:03:32.829 --> 00:03:37.932
"Go home and you will find what she wished for," said the fish.

55
00:03:38.852 --> 00:03:40.153
Then it swam away.

56
00:03:41.153 --> 00:03:47.017
When the man returned home, he was amazed to see that a fine new cottage had replaced his

57
00:03:47.097 --> 00:03:48.437
small, modest hut.

58
00:03:50.439 --> 00:03:52.840
Just then, his wife ran toward him.

59
00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:55.421
"Go back to the golden fish!"

60
00:03:55.941 --> 00:03:56.721
she demanded.

61
00:03:56.741 --> 00:04:01.662
"And tell the fish I want to be queen of this island!"

62
00:04:03.063 --> 00:04:07.724
Again the fisherman obeyed his wife's command and headed back to the sea.

63
00:04:07.744 --> 00:04:11.945
"Little fish, little fish," he called out.

64
00:04:13.646 --> 00:04:16.547
Soon the golden fish swam to the shore.

65
00:04:16.567 --> 00:04:19.348
"What do you want now, old man?"

66
00:04:21.788 --> 00:04:24.509
"My wife wants to be the queen of the island."

67
00:04:24.529 --> 00:04:30.150
"Go home and you will find what she wished for," said the fish.

68
00:04:31.311 --> 00:04:32.511
Then it swam away.

69
00:04:34.031 --> 00:04:39.233
When the fisherman arrived home, he stopped in his tracks and stared in amazement.

70
00:04:40.173 --> 00:04:46.555
A magnificent palace, bustling with guards, horses, and servants, had replaced the cottage!

71
00:04:47.995 --> 00:04:49.976
The old man entered the palace.

72
00:04:51.512 --> 00:04:57.277
Sitting on a golden throne, dressed in the elegant attire of a queen, was his wife.

73
00:04:57.297 --> 00:05:00.100
"Pardon me, wife?"

74
00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:02.001
The man spoke quietly.

75
00:05:02.021 --> 00:05:06.285
"Wife? How dare you address the queen as your wife!"

76
00:05:06.825 --> 00:05:08.006
she screamed loudly.

77
00:05:08.026 --> 00:05:11.770
"Guards! Take this disgusting man away!"

78
00:05:13.191 --> 00:05:15.433
The guards dragged the fisherman away.

79
00:05:16.914 --> 00:05:22.302
While his wife ruled the island, he spent his days sweeping the palace like a servant.

80
00:05:24.183 --> 00:05:27.265
Then one day the queen summoned the fisherman.

81
00:05:27.285 --> 00:05:29.726
"You old fool!"

82
00:05:30.246 --> 00:05:31.127
she ordered him.

83
00:05:31.147 --> 00:05:35.830
"Go back to that fish and tell him that I no longer want to be queen.

84
00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:40.052
Now I want to be the empress of the sea!"

85
00:05:40.072 --> 00:05:45.355
"What?" The man stared at his greedy wife in disbelief.

86
00:05:46.316 --> 00:05:49.954
"No," he refused, slowly shaking his head.

87
00:05:49.974 --> 00:05:52.857
"You already have more than you need."

88
00:05:52.877 --> 00:05:58.742
"Go to the fish or I will chop your head off!"

89
00:05:59.362 --> 00:06:00.423
threatened the queen.

90
00:06:01.644 --> 00:06:04.006
The fisherman was taken back to the sea.

91
00:06:04.026 --> 00:06:07.268
"Little fish, little fish."

92
00:06:08.229 --> 00:06:10.971
But this time the golden fish did not appear.

93
00:06:10.991 --> 00:06:16.216
"Little fish, little fish," the man called again.

94
00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:19.841
Still the golden fish did not answer.

95
00:06:21.061 --> 00:06:26.382
The old man called out a third time, "Little fish, little fish."

96
00:06:27.863 --> 00:06:33.544
Suddenly the sky turned dark and the waves in the sea crashed and roared.

97
00:06:35.105 --> 00:06:38.586
At last the golden fish swam up to the shore.

98
00:06:38.606 --> 00:06:41.006
"What do you want, old man?"

99
00:06:42.607 --> 00:06:46.828
The fisherman bent his head low and spoke in a trembling voice.

100
00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:53.682
"My my wife now she wants to be the empress of the sea."

101
00:06:54.642 --> 00:06:56.463
The fish did not say a word.

102
00:06:58.403 --> 00:07:03.124
Instead it simply turned and disappeared into the churning waters.

103
00:07:04.625 --> 00:07:08.526
When the old man returned home, he could not believe his eyes.

104
00:07:09.566 --> 00:07:11.767
The magnificent palace was gone.

105
00:07:12.347 --> 00:07:15.348
In its place stood their old modest hut.

106
00:07:16.532 --> 00:07:19.694
The fisherman and his wife returned to their former life.

107
00:07:21.115 --> 00:07:24.158
Every day the fisherman went fishing, as usual.

108
00:07:25.158 --> 00:07:29.201
But he never caught the extraordinary golden fish again.
